%-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Publications for the CV.
%
% Which list an entry goes into is set by `keywords`:
%   lead    -> Lead-author publications
%   contrib -> Contributed publications (co-author)
%   inprep  -> Manuscripts in preparation: kept here but not printed (the CV has
%              no In Preparation list); change to lead or contrib once published
% `addendum` holds the one-line "Contributions:" note printed under the entry.
%
% To add a paper: grab its BibTeX from INSPIRE
%   https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/<recid>?format=bibtex
% paste it here, add `keywords` and `addendum`, and shorten the author list:
%   lead:    author = "Zeng, J. and others"                ->  J. Zeng et al.
%   contrib: author = "First, A. and Zeng, J. and others"  ->  A. First, J. Zeng, et al.
% (the CV prints at most two names; my name is printed in bold)
% Within each list, keep entries newest first (they print in file order).
% arXiv-only papers: use the article type with `eprint` (as below), never misc --
% misc is the talk format of the CV and would print the paper as a talk.
% (No at-signs in these comments: bibtex reads every one as the start of an entry.)
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

